  "reason": "The abstract discusses models for predicting Torsades de Pointes (TdP) in humans using nonclinical assays. While it mentions that the variables used by each model have been reported to correlate with clinical outcome and that each model has been shown to discriminate between antiarrhythmic and nonarrhythmic drugs, it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity/specificity) between the animal model results and human clinical results. It is a review of models and their potential, but not a quantitative analysis of agreement."
